---
/**
 * Render source for `public/og.png` — the DEFAULT social card, used by every
 * page that does not pass its own `ogImage`. Homepage, blog index, everything.
 *
 * The card it replaces dated from July and had drifted twice over:
 *
 * 1. COPY. It read "The GTM OS for adtech startups". Base.astro's own comment
 *    calls that line retired — the hero and footer moved on and the card did
 *    not, so the whole site was sharing dead positioning every time a link was
 *    posted. The headline here is the live H1 from Hero.astro, verbatim, which
 *    is the same rule Base.astro's SITE_TITLE already follows.
 *
 * 2. FORMAT AND PALETTE. Same two problems the tool card had: 1200x630 is
 *    1.905:1 and X centre-crops anything that is not 2:1, and the cold
 *    ink-050/white/blue treatment predates the warm layer. See
 *    og-rank-my-adtech.astro for the full reasoning; this card is deliberately
 *    its sibling so the two read as one set.
 *
 * The mono status strip is kept VERBATIM from the old card. It is good, approved
 * brand furniture in the house's technical register, and none of what was wrong
 * with the card was wrong with that line.
 *
 * To re-render:  node scripts/render-og.mjs site
 */
import "../../styles/main.css";
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <title>OG — And/or Labs</title>
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="og">
      <div class="og__card">
        <header class="og__top">
          <span class="og__brand">And/or Labs</span>
          <span class="og__meta">EST. 2025 · CRT-01 <i class="og__dot"></i></span>
        </header>

        <h1 class="og__h">
          Don't just<br />go-to-market.<br /><em>Win it.</em>
        </h1>

        <footer class="og__foot">
          <span class="og__rule"></span>
          <p class="og__status">
            <span class="og__k">SYSCHECK</span>
            <span>positioning <b>OK</b></span>
            <span>distribution <b>OK</b></span>
            <span>pipeline <b>RUNNING</b></span>
          </p>
        </footer>
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  /* Fixed pixel values, not tokens — a 1200x600 canvas, not a responsive page.
     The COLOURS still come from tokens so the card cannot drift from the palette. */
  :global(body) { margin: 0; }
  :global(astro-dev-toolbar) { display: none !important; }

  .og {
    width: 1200px;
    height: 600px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 40px;
    background-color: var(--paper);
    display: flex;
  }
  .og__card {
    flex: 1;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    background: var(--surface-warm);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--ink-900);
    border-radius: 20px;
    box-shadow: 10px 10px 0 0 var(--ink-900);
    padding: 52px 56px 46px;
  }

  .og__top { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; }
  .og__brand {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 23px;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--blue-500);
  }
  /* Copper: a label on a warm surface, never an action. */
  .og__meta {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 16px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--copper-700);
  }
  .og__dot { width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--copper-600); }

  /* `margin: auto 0` centres the headline in the leftover height rather than
     hanging it off the top row with the slack collecting underneath. */
  .og__h {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: var(--weight-regular);
    font-size: 68px;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    /* Near-black on pink, per the warm-layer rule. */
    color: var(--text-on-warm);
    margin: auto 0;
  }
  .og__h em { font-style: normal; color: var(--blue-500); }

  .og__foot { margin-top: auto; }
  .og__rule { display: block; height: 1px; background: var(--border-warm); margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .og__status {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 34px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 19px;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    /* ink-500 goes hazy on pink; the warm layer has its own muted step. */
    color: var(--text-on-warm-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .og__k { color: var(--copper-700); letter-spacing: 0.12em; }
  .og__status b { font-weight: 400; color: var(--blue-500); }
</style>
